      "MISS TAYLOR: Time’s up! Everyone hand your work in.\nMISS TAYLOR: Lucinda, you need to finish up now.\nMISS TAYLOR: Oh Lucinda, the assignment was to draw a picture. This was your idea...\nPRINCIPAL: We, the students and faculty of Paul Revere Elementary...",
      "PRINCIPAL: ...hereby bury this time capsule in dedication of our new school, and we charge our descendants to open this vault of history fifty years fr…\nPRINCIPAL: To the future, and the promise it holds!\nMISS TAYLOR: Lucinda?\nMISS TAYLOR: LUCINDA!!!",
      "MISS TAYLOR: Lucinda! Thank God!\nMISS TAYLOR: What are you doing in here?\nLUCINDA: Stop it!... Stop talking!\nMISS TAYLOR: Lucinda... what on earth...",
      "PRINCIPAL: Fifty years ago the students and faculty of Paul Revere Elementary imagined what the future might hold. Today we unveil their legacy...\nPRINCIPAL: Now I’d like to introduce you to someone very special: Miss Priscilla Taylor. Since Miss Taylor was there for the original dedication, it’s …\nMISS TAYLOR: Just as my students fifty years ago looked to the future... let us now remember the past.",
      "DIANA: Abby! Now!\nABBY: It was nice meeting you."
    ]
